2 Experimental setup and research method description
At this initial stage of research, the fixed-pitch propeller with blades geometric twist was chosen as a research object. It is shown in Fig. 1.
Fig. 2 Experimental setup in the wind tunnel test chamber
Propeller radius is 90 mm, propeller pitch is 125.5 mm. Detailed propeller geometric characteristics are presented in Table 1. Propeller was mounted on the electric motor attached to the mechanical scales by which the propeller generated thrust was measured. This experimental setup was placed in the wind tunnel test chamber of Moscow State Technical University of Civil Aviation Aerodynamics and Aircraft Structures Department (Fig. 2). Wind tunnel was generating airflow blowing on the propeller. Scales were mounted on the rotatable base that could
