It should be also taken into account that in these conditions, helicopter airframe aerodynamic yaw moment My ha contributes to the occurrence of unanticipated yaw rotation (Fig. 6). These considerations suggest that helicopter wind blowing which decreases tail rotor blades angles of attack (against TR thrust vector) is more dangerous than blowing in the opposite direction which leads to the vortex ring state. In this regard, it is worth mentioning this paper authors experiments with a radio-controlled helicopter model in the wind tunnel which confirm this conclusion [23].
